    "Blinko" : {

    },
    "Blinko Settings" : {

    },
    "Blinko listens only while you are in a call and muted in the meeting app, and never records. It can't hear you when the microphone itself is muted (Blinko's Mute button mutes it for every app), so the warning covers mutes made inside the meeting app: Zoom (read from its menu, needs Accessibility), and apps that release the microphone while muted." : {

    },
    "Bluetooth devices" : {

    },
    "Bring the call to the front" : {

    },
    "Brings the call to the front (needs Accessibility to leave from here)" : {

    },
    "Browsers (Google Meet…)" : {

    },
    "Browsers count when a page uses the microphone (Google Meet, Teams or Zoom on the web); the calendar event happening now names the call. Leave uses Teams' and Slack's own shortcuts, and Zoom's (which asks to confirm), when Accessibility is granted; otherwise it brings the call to the front." : {

